WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.550
We've been wondering for a while now and sort
of asking questions about whether we can trust

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.990
the corona virus numbers that we're getting.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.590
And part of the reason why that's been in
question is that there have been reports that

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:18.039
individual states were choosing to suppress
data, maybe not so much about cases, but possibly

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:19.109
about deaths.

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:24.769
Florida was one place where we heard those
allegations made very specifically.

00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:29.140
But now we have to talk about this at the
federal level because there are growing reports

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:36.219
that the Trump administration is coordinating
a suppression effort to prevent the real numbers

00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:38.550
about Corona virus from getting out.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.930
And we've actually gotten our hands on a memo
that was sent out, which specifically says

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:50.969
to hospitals, as of today, July 15, stop sending
the data to the CDC.

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:57.039
Instead, send it to the Department of Health
and Human Services, run by Trump Tool and

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:00.570
sycophant Alex Azar.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:05.770
This is exactly what we predicted might happen
months ago if the numbers did not improve.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:10.630
The New York Times reported yesterday that
hospitals have been ordered to bypass the

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:11.700
normal process.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:17.439
The normal process is hospitals report to
the CDC and they were told, send us all of

00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:21.369
your data, send it directly to the Department
of Health and Human Services.

00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:23.680
This is the opposite of transparency.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.729
This opens the door to just hiding the data.

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:31.190
And health experts obviously are alarmed because
they know exactly how this can go.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:35.430
Now, we eventually got a copy of the order
from the Trump administration.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:40.641
And what the document says to hospitals is,
don't send your information to the CDC, send

00:01:40.641 --> 00:01:41.680
it to us.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.600
And of course, that is a department, the Department
of Health and Human Services, that is run

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.729
by the guy Trump picked and who has been brownnosing
Trump since the start of this pandemic.

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:58.400
And in all of history, since the CDC was created,
pandemic data, health data like what we're

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:05.109
dealing with today goes to the CDC, the Kaiser
Family Foundation, which has no connection

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:07.979
whatsoever to the insurance company Kaiser
Permanente.

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:13.170
The Kaiser Family Foundation says, quote,
This is Jen Kates, the director of Global

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.280
Health and HIV Policy.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.269
Jen Kates says, historically, the CDC has
been the place where public health data has

00:02:19.269 --> 00:02:20.480
been sent.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.620
And this raises questions.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.650
I love the understated nature.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:29.420
This raises questions about not just access
for researchers, but access for reporters,

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.159
access for the public to try to better understand
what is happening with the outbreak.

00:02:33.159 --> 00:02:35.690
How will the data be protected?

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:37.459
Will there be transparency?

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:39.290
Will there be access?

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:44.460
And what is the role of the CDC in understanding
the data?

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:50.880
Now, you need only zoom out like the tiniest
bit to understand what is most likely going

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:51.880
on here.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:58.670
Donald Trump admitted that he wanted to slow
down testing in order to cover up the reality

00:02:58.670 --> 00:02:59.670
of the pandemic.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:04.330
Rember, he said, one of the reasons we have
so many cases is we have so many tests.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.410
Now, this ignores a whole bunch of realities.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:12.750
In fact, if you don't test, it doesn't affect
the real number of cases, except it probably

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:17.060
increases the real number of cases because
without testing, people don't know they have

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.459
the virus and they go out and they spread
it.

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:23.170
So not testing actually spreads the disease.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:27.810
Additionally, as testing has gone up in many
of the states that are worst affected, the

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.000
positivity rate has gone up.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.950
If you go from 5000 to 10000 tests a day and
you go from having two percent of the people

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:40.310
test positive to four percent, that is a signal
of a growing epidemic.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.069
This is all way beyond Donald Trump.

00:03:42.069 --> 00:03:44.150
He doesn't seem to understand any of this
stuff.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:49.610
So the point is, once you understand, Trump
admitted to wanting to slow down testing,

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:53.810
to slow down case numbers, and you see that
the Trump administration is saying the hospitals

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.239
don't send your data to the CDC.

00:03:56.239 --> 00:03:59.030
Send your data to Alex Azar at HHS.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:04.709
The obvious next step is to start covering
up this data, cover up death data, cover up

00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:06.380
hospitalization data.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:12.310
The White House is trying to muzzle the normal
reporting process, and the only reason that

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:16.470
that exists is to suppress information.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:20.090
If he can't stop the testing, he'll stop the
information.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:22.940
Now, I'm hoping I don't I don't know.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.560
I've talked to a few people today and they
have different opinions that could this work

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:31.770
because there are other ways to get the data
out.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:37.700
Media will talk to hospitals and hospitals
will say, well, we'll say we're full.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:40.940
We have no room in the ICU, for example.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:47.200
And at a certain point, if the data that the
Trump administration is allowing to be published

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:53.690
says one thing that goes completely against
what the ICU information is, at a certain

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:57.000
point, you would hope that it would explode.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.760
That the real data has been covered up.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:00.760
I don't know.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.990
I mean, I'm hopeful that this can't really
be covered up to this degree, but the administration

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:10.230
has decided the numbers must go down, that
the numbers have to go down for the benefit

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:11.960
of Donald Trump's reelection.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.380
Here's one way to do it.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:20.550
Now, what we can hope for is that we still
find the data and that Trump is punished electorally

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:25.730
for trying to suppress the data rather than
dealing with the pandemic itself.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:29.630
It's too early to know which way it will go
because the directive starts today.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.450
It's effective as of July 15th.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:33.300
So we'll have to see what happens.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:37.660
But what we need to understand is that from
this point forward, from as if this wasn't

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:42.530
already the case in many of the states in
the United States already from this point

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:49.340
forward, we have to realize that the numbers
that make it out may not be the real numbers,

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:57.041
because the idea is hide the data to justify
a faster economic opening to help Donald Trump

00:05:57.041 --> 00:05:58.440
get himself reelected.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:02.970
His reelection is the most important factor.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:05.590
It's far more important than American lives.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:10.320
And it's really the only thing you need to
know to understand how to analyze the actions

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:11.970
of this administration.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.120
It seems to run counter to health.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.390
It seems to run counter to common sense.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:21.720
It seems short sighted in terms of the economy
because the relapse effect will hurt the economy.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:25.710
You just have to understand, Trump thinks
it might help him get reelected in November.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:26.810
That's all that's going on.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:32.080
The pandemic response has been blown so badly
that there's really no way to fix it before

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.080
the election.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:36.610
I was looking at some data today, and this
is important for you to understand.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:41.401
When New York hit its peak right around April
twelve, April 15, something like that, that's

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:43.900
when New York had its peak of cases.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:50.080
It took two full months with strict lockdowns
for New York cases to come down.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:54.850
Remember that deaths lag cases by about 15
to 20 days.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:55.850
So by.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:07:02.740
April, May, June, by mid-June, you finally
had this improving in New York.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:08.660
And only in the last 10 days in July have
New York's death numbers really finished coming

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:13.130
down to, you know, a number that hopefully
they won't spike again from.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:19.060
So you take that model two months for cases
and then another fifteen or so days, four

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.060
deaths.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:26.280
If Arizona and Florida and Texas fully locked
down today, if they don't even want you.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:32.270
But if they did that, you're looking at September
15th to get cases under control and October

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:37.280
1st to get what is the coming spike of deaths
back under control.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:38.630
They're not willing to do it.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:39.630
I mean, yeah.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:40.810
Greg Abbott now is saying more.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.670
You've got to wear a mask.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:47.040
But these are not places that seem to have
an appetite politically or economically or

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.740
in any other way for a full lockdown.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.840
So Trump recognizes the numbers aren't going
to be under control.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:59.140
When you get to 10, 15000 cases a day, that
doesn't just go away in two weeks.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:04.570
They are going to be dealing with widespread
outbreaks until close to election time if

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:07.050
we have the surging second wave.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.740
By then, it could be even worse.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:13.780
We're now hearing from the CDC that this fall
may be one of the most difficult times in

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:14.780
American history.

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:17.020
From the standpoint of public health.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.390
So what can Trump do?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.390
Just lie.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.390
Cover up the data.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.940
That's all that they can do to hide the data.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.220
Use the data.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:29.110
We'll use the data you're willing to publish,
which is not accurate to say we should reopen

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:34.510
re-open in order to make things seem normal
so that people will vote for you in the fall.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.030
Hopefully the real data makes it out.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:43.820
But this is now taking on the sort of color
of a full cover up because the actual remember,

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:48.890
it would have been rather than covering up
data, changing reporting procedure, all of

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:49.890
the stuff.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:54.360
It would have been much easier to just deal
with the virus from the get go.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:56.390
That's not what this administration chose
to do.

